<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

  <!-- ================================================================================================
       THE MENU APPEARANCE — a REPRODUCTION of EmberTern's, not a link, and not an invention.

       ⭐⭐ Why this file exists at all. The License Manager gained a hamburger menu (L6.1a) and had
       ZERO menu styling — no `ContextMenu`, no `MenuItem`, no `Separator`, and no menu anywhere in the
       application. Without these, Avalonia falls back to FluentTheme's own: 27 px rows, 14 pt type, and
       hover/selection painted from `SystemAccentColor` — the brown/orange the palette fights everywhere
       else (CLAUDE.md styling rule 6). That is the identical situation §40.2 recorded when it declined a
       `TabControl` for the view switch.

       ⚠⚠ THE HONEST STATUS: this is a COPY, and a copy drifts. The project's own answer to that problem
       twice — `IconGeometries.axaml` (L5.1) and `DataGridStyles.axaml` (L5.4) — was to SPLIT the block
       out of `EmberTern.App` and LINK it, and that remains the better move. It was measured and offered:
       the source block is type-free, token-only and sits at the very END of `ControlStyles.axaml`, so the
       split is a clean cut of the file's tail. ⛔ The user ratified the copy instead (decision D‑7 = B)
       to keep `EmberTern.App` closed during this stage.

       ⭐ SO THE DRIFT IS GUARDED INSTEAD: `MenuStyleDriftTests` compares this file against
       `src/EmberTern.App/Themes/ControlStyles.axaml` selector by selector and setter by setter, resolving
       tokens to their values first. It fails if a setter here disagrees with EmberTern's, if EmberTern
       gains a menu selector this file has not decided about, or if this file invents one of its own.
       ⛔ Do not "fix" a failure there by editing the expectation — the point is that the two must agree.

       ── The two deliberate differences, both recorded so the guard can allow exactly them ──

       1. ⛔ `MenuItem /template/ TextBlock#PART_InputGestureText` is NOT reproduced. It styles the
          keyboard-gesture column, and the License Manager has no command registry, no gesture vocabulary
          and no menu row that shows one. Copying it would be carrying chrome for a surface that does not
          exist — and gotcha #233's dead-surface trap is exactly that.

       2. ⭐ Two literals in EmberTern's block are written HERE AS THE TOKENS THAT ALREADY NAME THEM, at
          identical rendered values: `Pad.MenuItem` IS `10,3` and `Border.All` IS `1` (both measured in
          `Tokens.axaml`). ⚠ That is not a cosmetic improvement — this application's
          `LicenseManagerThemeTests.NoMetricIsWrittenAsALiteralWhereATokenNamesIt` has no per-file
          allowance list, so it is STRICTER than the guard EmberTern applies to its own file, and a
          verbatim copy would fail the build.

       ⚠ The five remaining literals have no token and deliberately do not gain one: inventing a
       `Thickness` role for one element would be starting the ratified spacing stage through the back
       door, which `SettingsWindow.axaml` in EmberTern refuses in those exact words. They are listed with
       their reasons in the theme guard's allowance table.
       ================================================================================================ -->

  <Style Selector="ContextMenu">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SurfaceRaisedBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="{DynamicResource Border.All}" />
    <!-- ⚠ 4 stays, DELIBERATELY, and EmberTern carries the same note: a context menu floats above the
         content, while `Radius.Surface` is 3. ⛔ Not `Radius.Chip` or `Radius.Tab` — both happen to be 4
         today, and borrowing an unrelated role because its number matches is how a role stops meaning
         anything. The open question "floating surface: 3 or 4?" belongs to product-polish §13.3. -->
    <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="4" />
    <!-- A 4px band top and bottom so the first and last row do not touch the border. -->
    <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0,4" />
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Text.Application.Size}" />
  </Style>

  <Style Selector="ContextMenu, MenuItem">
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource ForegroundBrush}" />
  </Style>

  <!-- The row. 12px type and a symmetric 3px vertical pad bring a row from Fluent's 27px to ~22px
       without crowding the text; MinHeight keeps an icon-less row exactly as tall as one with an icon. -->
  <Style Selector="MenuItem">
    <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Text.Application.Size}" />
    <Setter Property="Padding" Value="{DynamicResource Pad.MenuItem}" />
    <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="22" />
  </Style>

  <Style Selector="MenuItem /template/ Border#PART_LayoutRoot">
    <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="{DynamicResource Radius.Surface}" />
    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="3,0" />
  </Style>

  <!-- Hover / open-submenu / pressed. One calm wash from the app's palette; never SystemAccentColor. -->
  <Style Selector="MenuItem:pointerover /template/ Border#PART_LayoutRoot">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource HoverOverlayBrush}" />
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="MenuItem:selected /template/ Border#PART_LayoutRoot">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SelectionBrush}" />
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="MenuItem:pressed /template/ Border#PART_LayoutRoot">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SelectionBrush}" />
  </Style>

  <!-- ⭐⭐ A disabled item still has to be READABLE — and in this application that is load-bearing rather
       than a nicety: `About` ships as a deliberate disabled placeholder (D‑8's sibling decision), so the
       disabled state is not an edge case here, it is a row the operator sees on every open. Fluent's
       default fades it close to invisible. -->
  <Style Selector="MenuItem:disabled /template/ Border#PART_LayoutRoot">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
  </Style>
  <Style Selector="MenuItem:disabled">
    <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource SubtleForegroundBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.75" />
  </Style>

  <!-- The icon column: a fixed 14px box so every mark reads at one size regardless of its geometry's
       proportions, with breathing room before the label. -->
  <Style Selector="MenuItem /template/ ContentControl#PART_IconPresenter">
    <Setter Property="Width" Value="14" />
    <Setter Property="Height" Value="14" />
    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="0,0,4,0" />
  </Style>

  <!-- Separator: a hairline that spans the menu, with equal air above and below. Scoped to menus so a
       Separator used elsewhere is untouched. -->
  <Style Selector="ContextMenu > Separator, MenuItem > Separator">
    <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource BorderBrush}" />
    <Setter Property="Height" Value="1" />
    <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="1" />
    <Setter Property="Margin" Value="6,4" />
    <Setter Property="Opacity" Value="0.7" />
  </Style>

</Styles>
